Z||000000||Simple Fiero||08-21-2001||12:38 PM||||K my gas gauge is not working properly, so I have been watching my trip odo. But here is my questions how high can i go on my trip, I have been filling up at 150 - 200. But something tells me that I can go a lot further than that. But I don't want to drain my tank right out, to find out. Also what does the Trip Odo measure in kms, miles, or wheel rotations, or what?(remember I am in Canada). <P>88 SC 4 Cyl||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gomez||08-21-2001||12:48 PM||||Well as for how far you can go thAT depends on the engine and shape of the car. If your car is originally a canadian car the trip reads in km if it was an american sold car it reads in miles.<BR>Randy||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||08-21-2001||01:01 PM||||Give it a "Dry Tank" drive... when you get to the 150-200 mark, carry a small (1 gal?) tank of Gas with, when it runs out- you'll know exactly how far you can go!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I heard somewhere that Jay Leno had a job doing this for and Old Rich Guy when he was a teenager!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||08-21-2001||03:19 PM||||My 86 v6's can get 250 kms to a tank and my old 85 4cy would get 350+ kms to a tank of gas. also when the tank is low and you stop hard or turn hard you can hear (louder humming noise) the pump cavitate (sucking air) so I know I need gas soon.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-21-2001||06:16 PM||||I would not drive for extended periods low on fuel the gas in the tank keeps pump cool.If you are taking a long trip stop and get gas often I learned this the hard way on a trip from Wis. to AZ.My fuel pump gave up its ghost in Nm. this was not fun.There were also other cars at the same repair shop Gm cars I might add with pumps in the tanks all with toasted pumps in them Just my 7 cents worth||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mickey_Moose||08-21-2001||06:30 PM||||heh...not all Canadian cars read kilometers...we have one member in our club that the speedo is in km and the odometer is in miles - go figure.<P>Tim||||reg||1
Z||000006||Kasdan||08-23-2001||09:02 AM||||My 86 GT can only get approx 15MPG...10 gallon tank....you do the math...<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, Holley Ram-Air<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
